{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2202","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Parkour Design"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Today, Alex wants to build a parkour course for Steve to train his parkour skills on. A "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"parkour course"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a sequence $$$p_0 \\to p_1 \\to \\ldots \\to p_k$$$ of integer coordinates on the plane. Here, a contiguous pair of coordinates is called a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"move"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", denoted as $$$p_{i-1} \\to p_i$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alex knows that Steve can only perform the following types of moves:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$(x_i,y_i) \\to (x_i+2,y_i+1)$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$(x_i,y_i) \\to (x_i+3,y_i)$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$(x_i,y_i) \\to (x_i+4,y_i-1)$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that Steve will not perform any other type of moves. For example, Steve can perform $$$(0,0) \\to (2,1)$$$ and $$$(2,1) \\to (5,1)$$$, but will "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"never"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" perform moves such as $$$(2,1) \\to (3,2)$$$, $$$(3,0) \\to (5,-1)$$$, or $$$(4,-1) \\to (6,-1)$$$ (even though they may look very easy)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an integer coordinate $$$(x,y)$$$ on the plane."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Please determine if it is possible to make a parkour course $$$q_0,q_1,\\ldots,q_k$$$ that satisfies the following conditions:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$q_0=(0,0)$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$q_k=(x,y)$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The parkour course "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"only consists of"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" moves that Steve can perform. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^3$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of each test case contains two integers $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$ ($$$1 \\le x \\le 10^9$$$, $$$-10^8 \\le y \\le 10^8$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If it is possible to make a parkour course that satisfies the conditions, output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" on a separate line."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If it is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"impossible"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" to make a parkour course that satisfies the conditions, output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" on a separate line."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can output the answer in any case. For example, the strings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yEs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" will also be recognized as positive responses."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n11\n2 1\n3 0\n4 -1\n4 1\n14 1\n1 -4\n3 -1\n2 10\n24 -1\n24 -3\n8 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\nYES\nYES\nNO\nYES\nNO\nNO\nNO\nNO\nYES\nYES\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the fifth test case, the parkour course must start from $$$(0,0)$$$ and end on $$$(14,1)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This can be achieved by the following parkour course."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$$$$(0,0) \\to (4,-1) \\to (7,-1) \\to (9,0) \\to (12,0) \\to (14,1)$$$$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that the following parkour course "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"does not"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" satisfy the third condition stated above due to the moves highlighted in red."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$$$$(0,0) \\to \\color{red}{(4,-1) \\to (6,-1)} \\to (8,0) \\to \\color{red}{(11,0) \\to (14,1)}$$$$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"2202A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2202/problem/A"}